  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Cup descriptions in the lending record are sufficient to match returns without storing personal contact details.\", \"decision\": \"How should returned cups be matched to the lending record?\", \"goal\": \"Make cup lending and return convenient while keeping the available stock and volunteer work understandable.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood café wants to lend reusable cups at community gatherings and recover them afterward. It has a modest cup stock, washable collection crates, a simple lending record, and volunteers who can share short shifts. The plan concerns a small pilot with no deposit or sales system. Different decisions address separate moments in lending, return, and review.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nGuests point out the matching cup description in the lending record, and a volunteer confirms the return. Borrowers help locate their entries while volunteers verify them.\nVolunteers gather a small crate of returns and then match all its cup descriptions to the lending record. Recording is concentrated into short batches.\nVolunteers match each cup description to the lending record before adding the cup to a return crate. The outstanding list changes immediately at intake."
    }
  ],
